{
 "name": "layer-b",
 "seed": 1,
 "duration": 4200,
 "comment": "Layer B on the single-server shape (deploy-q5 design \u00a73.3; shared-cells PLAN \u00a74.1): 1,000 projects. Setup 0-600 s, the compliant classes 600-4200 s, the hostile classes from 1800 s. The victim's period solo is 900-1800 s, noisy 2100-4200 s. Writers stop 60 s before the readers of their window, so a subscriber cut at the end has read everything it was sent. Quota posture, both in this one manifest (lead decision deploy-q5 #6 (1), 2026-10-13): the compliant classes, the victim, the h11t-fresh target and the idle classes are admitted at the cell's ceilings (no quota set) as the stress, the hostile ones at q-hostile and again at the ceilings, and free-tier twins of S0, S1 (batched), S2, S3s, N0 and the victim at the issuer's free-tier table (quota set free-tier: requests_per_sec 10, the other axes at the ceilings; owner decision I7 (a)). A free-tier project's request bucket and store budget each hold one second of its rate. k2gen's appends are an open-loop Poisson process, so each twin's aggregate mean (appends, pulls, settles, reads and SSE connects) is at most 5 requests a second: simulated against that bucket, a mean of 8 refuses about 0.3% and 5 or less none. A consumer group's appends each bring a pull's return and a settle within milliseconds, so its Poisson clusters come three times over: a twin with a group appends at most 0.1 times a second and starts its consumers a second apart. Every twin creates its streams a second apart and none deletes. A create weighs 11 of the store budget's 10 a second, and a project's first create since its cell booted 21 (it also lists the project's streams to seed its max_streams count), so each twin's second create is refused once at setup: known red until the owner decides (bench/k2cost/README.md, 'Known red'). An honest refusal that survives this shaping is a PB-E3 finding. cold makes room for the twins, so the manifest keeps 1,000 projects (rc-certify's MIN_PROJECTS). shared_verdict.py records the posture in the arm manifest.",
 "periods": {
  "solo": [
   900,
   1800
  ],
  "noisy": [
   2100,
   4200
  ]
 },
 "quota_sets": {
  "q-hostile": {
   "requests_per_sec": 20,
   "append_bytes_per_sec": 64000,
   "append_records_per_sec": 200,
   "read_bytes_per_sec": 256000,
   "max_inflight_requests": 8,
   "max_live_subscriptions": 16,
   "max_streams": 50,
   "queued_append_bytes": 1048576
  },
  "free-tier": {
   "requests_per_sec": 10
  }
 },
